## Original Content
What a new round of U.S. sanctions could mean after nearly six months of war with Iran — and years of economic pressure on the country.

## Summary
This article explores whether a new round of U.S. sanctions can succeed in pressuring Iran where military airstrikes and diplomatic negotiations have failed. It discusses the potential impact of escalating economic warfare after years of conflict and pressure.

## Key Points
- The U.S. is escalating economic pressure on Iran with a new round of sanctions.
- Previous military actions like airstrikes and diplomatic efforts such as negotiations have not achieved desired outcomes with Iran.
- Economic sanctions are being tested as an alternative strategy in the ongoing 'economic war' against Iran.


